# generated/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It once was, on the assumption that anything regenerable is disposable. Two
# parts of the framework now depend on those files being committed:
#
#   - the `no-drift` CI gate runs every generator with --check and compares the
#     output against what is in the repository. With nothing to compare
#     against, the gate cannot fail -- which is worse than not having it.
#   - the deploy scripts read from generated/, so a CI deploy job needs the
#     artefacts present.
#
# The diffs are also the point: a changed measure or a moved visual shows up as
# a few readable lines in a pull request rather than as an opaque redeploy.

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
